        "风险管理团队"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "Signification of Abbreviations: RE=Risk Evaluation; S=Severity (1 negligible; 2 minor; 3 Serious; 4 Critical; 5 Catastrophic); P=The probability of a harm occurring (6 Frequent; 5 Probable; 4 Occasional; 3 Remote; 2 Improbable; 1 Few); R=Risk NO.; ACC=Acceptable; NACC=Unacceptable; PRM=Plan of Risk control measure(s); NH=New hazard generated; N/A=Not apply; Y=Yes; N=No; AFAP=As far as possible without adversely affecting the benefit-risk ratio.",
      "topic_tags": [
