    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "In summary, all individual risks are acceptable after implementation of risk control measures. According to ISO 14971:2019 section 7.4 'Benefit-risk analysis: If a residual risk is not judged acceptable using the criteria established in the risk management plan and further risk control is not practicable, the manufacturer may gather and review data and literature to determine if the benefits of the intended use outweigh this residual risk.' So there is no need to do a risk benefit analysis for above risks.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "ISO 14971:2019",
        "benefit-risk analysis",
        "residual risk",
        "risk acceptance"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Risk Analysis Report",
        "Risk Management Plan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "Residual risk evaluation and conclusion: According to the risk acceptance table, the risk levels after control are described as follows. All single residual risks are in the 'Acceptable' area. Distribution: R19,R25,R29,R30,R31,R34,R38,R39,R40,R41,R42,R43,R44,R47,R48,R49,R52,R53 are at probability=2(Improbable)/severity=3(Serious); R23,R36 are at probability=1(Few)/severity=2(Minor); R9,R10,R11,R12,R13,R15,R16,R17,R18,R20,R21,R22,R24,R26,R27,R28,R32,R33,R35,R37,R45,R46,R50,R51,R54 are at probability=1(Few)/severity=3(Serious); R1,R2,R3,R4,R5,R6,R7,R8,R14 are at probability=1(Few)/severity=4(Critical). The distribution of all the residual risks less than 1/2 of the overall residual risks are in the higher severity regions or in the higher probability regions. And the clusters of all the residual risks are not borderline. So the overall residual risks are also acceptable.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "residual risk",
        "risk matrix",
        "risk acceptance",
        "overall residual risk"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Risk Analysis Report",
        "Risk Management Plan",
